  "step_3": "The decision reason requires that the individual considers the probabilities of favorable outcomes and prefers the lottery with a higher such probability. In this case, Lottery B has a 100% probability of a favorable outcome (2400 Euros), while Lottery A has only a 67% chance of a favorable outcome (66% for 2400, 1% for 2500). Thus, Lottery B has a higher probability of a favorable outcome. However, the verbal report does not mention probabilities at all. Instead, it focuses on the small differences in gains and justifies the choice by saying the risk of losing everything is not justified. This indicates that the individual did not consider or apply the rule about comparing probabilities of favorable outcomes. Therefore, the decision reason was not used in the deliberation process.",
